The Unicode tables core measures text with, in dist/unicode.generated.js, are
generated by the Loom repository's scripts/generate-unicode-tables.mjs from
the data files of @rockorager/uucode 2.2.1, which derive from Unicode 17 data.
The generator writes the same values as a JavaScript module, so a bundle
carries them.

The grapheme width iterator in dist/style-width.js is ported from the
@rockorager/uucode 2.2.1 width module. Changes made to it:

- It is written in TypeScript and reads the generated tables module.
- It yields each grapheme's start, end, and width, and no longer yields the
  grapheme's text or offers clone, peek, or a standalone string width.
